# The 287 around a signal's handler (roadmap os-server.md P10): init starts
# tests/posix/sigfpu.c (TEST_POSIX_SIGFPU), an executable marked as using
# the 287 (mkexe --287, RXF_287), whose handler spoils the 287's control
# word and stack; the trampoline's FSAVE and FRSTOR keep them. (MAME has
# no 287.)
program: idle
define: TEST_POSIX_SIGFPU
keys: {wait 250}
match: contains
timeout: 120
emulators: bochs dosbox-x
---
sigfpu: spoilt by a call (0): 0
sigfpu: around a handler, the control word and pi kept (3): 3
sigfpu: done
